#NEXUS

[ torcidafernández-baldor2011a_fig14: Diplodocoid strict consensus (panel A). Topology from the PDF's vector paths, read junction by junction because lines run through verticals: the Diplodocus branch is the continuation of the flagellicaudatan stem, the Dicraeosaurus-row line enters the dicraeosaurid node, and the Zapalasaurus and Demandasaurus lines carry the rebbachisaurid stems. Every junction checked against panel C, which has the same topology except within Rebbachisauridae (A's strict consensus collapses it to a polytomy). 16 tips, 3 polytomies (4, 3, 5 children). Random-sample case (seed 20261114). Topology read from the PDF's own vector branch lines (each edge a stroked path from child to parent junction) and checked against the figure; tip names read from the figure; topology only. ]

BEGIN TAXA;
    DIMENSIONS NTAX=16;
    TAXLABELS
        Omeisaurus
        Jobaria
        Macronaria
        Suuwassea
        Apatosaurus
        Diplodocus
        Amargasaurus
        Brachytrachylopan
        Dicraeosaurus
        Histriasaurus
        Limaysaurus
        Rebbachisaurus
        Cathartesaura
        Zapalasaurus
        Nigersaurus
        Demandasaurus
    ;
END;

BEGIN TREES;
    TREE 'torcidafernández-baldor2011a_fig14' = [&R] (Omeisaurus,Jobaria,Macronaria,((Suuwassea,(Apatosaurus,Diplodocus),(Amargasaurus,(Brachytrachylopan,Dicraeosaurus))),(Histriasaurus,(Limaysaurus,Rebbachisaurus,Cathartesaura,Zapalasaurus,(Nigersaurus,Demandasaurus)))));
END;
